---
/**
 * On every preparedness page (spec §9 safety rule 5). Community resources come first, framed as
 * primary rather than a fallback.
 */
---
<aside class="rounded-md border-2 border-ink p-4 text-sm text-ink" aria-label="Get help">
  <p class="font-semibold">Start with your community.</p>
  <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1">
    <li><strong>Emergency:</strong> call 911.</li>
    <li><strong>Local help and services:</strong> call or text 211, or visit <a class="underline" href="https://www.211.org/">211.org</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Plans for where you live:</strong> contact your city or county emergency management office and sign up for its alerts.</li>
  </ul>
</aside>
